# NuGet Packaging Rules

## Packable packages (6)

All under `src/` — auto-detected by `Directory.Build.props` (`IsPackable=true`).

## Packaging config

- Output: `packages/` via `build/package.props`
- Symbols: `.snupkg` with SourceLink
- README: per-project `README.md` packed automatically
- Version: GitVersion (Conventional Commits)

## Pre-publish checklist

- [ ] Public API has XML documentation
- [ ] No dependency on `demos/` or `tests/` from `src/`
- [ ] No breaking changes without explicit note
- [ ] `dotnet test` passes; coverage meets assembly threshold
- [ ] `dotnet pack -c Release` without warnings

## API evolution

Prefer additive APIs, extensibility points, optional behaviors.
Avoid redesigning public APIs without strong justification.

See `.cursor/docs/08-nuget-checklist.md` for full review template.
